# Percentage division round-trip with a plain divisor

Verifies division by and with a percentage in both operand orders. Dividing decimal 100% by plain 3 keeps the percentage subtype and its decimal precision, while dividing plain 100 by that percentage scales the divisor by hundredths and returns the plain decimal inverse.

>>> source
third: decimal = 100% / 3
print(third)
restored: decimal = 100 / third
print(restored)

<<< stdout
33.3333%
300.0000

<<< stderr
